This extension adds HITMAN World of Assassination modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]SMF installed automatically.[/summary]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Steam Demo[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Xbox[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Simple Mod Framework mods with a "Deploy.exe" file install to the "Simple Mod Framework" folder.[/*]
[*]SMF mods with a "manifest.json" file and a ".rpkg" file install to the "Vortex_Mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Any other mod not described above installs to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Deploying only places each mod in the "Vortex_Mods" folder. Simple Mod Framework still has to install them before they do anything in game.[/*]
[*]Open Simple Mod Framework, press its "Add a Mod" button and pick the archive for the mod you want. The framework unpacks it and adds it to its own mod list, where you can enable it and set the load order.[/*]
[*]The notification shown after deploying has buttons to launch Simple Mod Framework and to open the "Vortex_Mods" folder. Both are also on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Leave Simple Mod Framework's own "Mods" folder alone. The framework reads every entry in it as a mod, so adding files there by hand stops it from starting.[/*]
[*]Simple Mod Framework's installer is downloaded once from its Nexus Mods page so the page gets the download credit. It is not run, and it is not needed - the framework itself is installed from its official release.[/*]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for HITMAN World of Assassination mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Simple Mod Framework:

Recognised when the archive contains a "Deploy.exe" file.

  Installs to: "Simple Mod Framework"

========================================================================

SMF Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a "manifest.json" file and a ".rpkg" file.

  Installs to: "Vortex_Mods"

========================================================================

Fallback Installer:

The catch-all. Any archive that matched none of the installers above lands here and is copied across unchanged.

[b][color=#ffff00]NOTE: Landing in the fallback installer is a signal your archive layout needs fixing.[/color][/b]

  Requirements:
    - Reaching this installer usually means the archive was not laid out in a way Vortex recognised.
    - Vortex shows the user a notification when a mod installs through the fallback.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - If your mod lands here unintentionally, re-check the layouts above - users will see a fallback warning and may report the mod as broken.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]

